  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Investments for prevention of loss and damage in Malawi - CCASE</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed project will undertake activities targeting 12,000 vulnerable households to build anticipatory, absorptive, adaptive, and transformative capacities in Neno District in Southern Malawi. The project will finance risk reduction measures to avert, minimise and address Loss and Damage. The project seeks to strengthen national and local resilience to disaster risks within the context of preventing loss and damage and ensuring sustainable development by working closely with Malawi Government through DODMA, EAD and DCCMS. Key support will be provided for activities that cost-effectively prevent or reduce low-level weather-related risks.</narrative>
  </description>
